196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 98 0 R
/T (Our investigation covered four areas. First, we analysed the Canny algorithm itself, stage by stage, to understand which parts map naturally onto hardware and which parts resist it. Second, we studied the streaming design techniques that HLS image pipelines rely on, since an FPGA cannot simply hold a frame in memory and loop over it the way software does. Third, we examined the KV260 platform to understand how work should be divided between its ARM processors and its FPGA fabric. Finally, we reviewed existing open-source HLS implementations of Canny as background reading, to sanity-check our architectural thinking against designs that have actually been built)
/E (Our investigation covered four areas. First, we analysed the Canny algorithm itself, stage by stage, to understand which parts map naturally onto hardware and which parts resist it. Second, we studied the streaming design techniques that HLS image pipelines rely on, since an FPGA cannot simply hold a frame in memory and loop over it the way software does. Third, we examined the KV260 platform to understand how work should be divided between its ARM processors and its FPGA fabric. Finally, we reviewed existing open-source HLS implementations of Canny as background reading, to sanity-check our architectural thinking against designs that have actually been built)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
